        "sha256": "764c6ad684e71e69425a9cfb0dae7e2384910499632670a07a5e7b2104d6bdd3",
        "signing_date": "1961-05-04",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10938.txt",
        "text_sha256": "1aa169fd7ab86861456343c959826ed09dba3a2c87185ed921e72a8cbb098586",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1961-05-06/pdf/FR-1961-05-06.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Section  1. There is hereby estab­\nlished the President’ s Foreign Intelli­\ngence Advisory Board. The function of \nthe Board shall be to advise the President \nwith respect to the objectives and con­\nduct of the foreign intelligence and re­\nlated activities— of the United States \nwhich are required in the interests of \nforeign policy and national defense and \nsecurity."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 1998,
      "char_start": 1121,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:10938#sec2",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Sec. 2.",
      "pdf_page": 3,
      "scope_id": "EO:10938#sec2",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "26 FR 3951, PDF pages 3-3",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "764c6ad684e71e69425a9cfb0dae7e2384910499632670a07a5e7b2104d6bdd3",
        "signing_date": "1961-05-04",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10938.txt",
        "text_sha256": "1aa169fd7ab86861456343c959826ed09dba3a2c87185ed921e72a8cbb098586",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1961-05-06/pdf/FR-1961-05-06.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Sec. 2. In the performance of its ad­\nvisory duties, the Board shall conduct a \ncontinuing review and assessment of all \nfunctions of the Central Intelligence \nA gency, and of other executive depart­\nm ents and agencies having such or \nsimilar responsibilities in the foreign \nintelligence and related fields, and shall \nreport thereon to the President each six \nmonths or more frequently as deemed \nappropriate. The Director of Central In­\ntelligence and the heads of other depart­\nments and agencies concerned shall make \navailable to the Board any information \nwith respect to foreign intelligence mat­\nters which the Board may require for the \npurpose of carrying out its responsibili­\nties to the President. The information \nso supplied to the Board shall be afforded \nrequisite security.  protection as pre­\nscribed by the provisions of applicable \nlaw s and regulations."
    },
    {
      "char_end": 2868,
      "char_start": 1999,
      "id": "CLAUSES:EO:10938#sec3",
      "kind": "section",
      "label": "Sec. 3.",
      "pdf_page": 3,
      "scope_id": "EO:10938#sec3",
      "source": {
        "filing_date": null,
        "location_confidence": "high",
        "location_verified": false,
        "page_or_item": "26 FR 3951, PDF pages 3-3",
        "requires_page_check": false,
        "sha256": "764c6ad684e71e69425a9cfb0dae7e2384910499632670a07a5e7b2104d6bdd3",
        "signing_date": "1961-05-04",
        "text_path": "jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_10938.txt",
        "text_sha256": "1aa169fd7ab86861456343c959826ed09dba3a2c87185ed921e72a8cbb098586",
        "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1961-05-06/pdf/FR-1961-05-06.pdf"
      },
      "text": "Sec. 3. Members of the Board shall be \nappointed from among qualified persons \noutside the Government and shall re­\nceive such compensation and allowances, \nconsonant with law, as may be prescribed \nhereafter. Such compensation and al­\nlowances and any other expenses arising \nin connection with the work of the Board \nshall be paid from the appropriation ap­\npearing under the heading “Special \nProjects” in title I of the General \nGovernment Matters Appropriation Act, \n1961,74 Stat. 473, and, to the extent per­\nmitted by law, from any corresponding \nappropriation which may be made for\nsubsequent years. Such payments shall \nbe made without regard to the provisions \nof section 3681 of thq Revised Statutes \nand section 9 of the act of March 4,1909, \n35 Stat. 1027 (31 U.S.C. 672 and 673).\nS ec. 4. Executive Order No. 10656 of \nFebruary 6, 1956, is hereby revoked."
    }
  ],
